# This machine's overlay location, written by tools/install.sh. Every machine has its
# own; the tracked axon.toml carries only a neutral default, so no machine ever has to
# edit a shared file. See schemas/machine.toml.example.
axon.local.toml

# Bazel's convenience symlinks (bazel-bin, bazel-out, bazel-testlogs, bazel-<workspace>).
# Kept after PRD Q44 retired Bazel (2026-08-25): every checkout that ever ran it still has
# them on disk, and an untracked symlink into a stale output tree must not become a tracked
# file. Anchored to the repo root, where they live — unanchored, this pattern also swallowed
# two real directories that were linked from the README and shipped in ARCHITECTURE.md while
# never being in the repo at all.
/bazel-*
.DS_Store
**/target/
**/node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# graphify's node IDs are slugified from the ABSOLUTE scan path (confirmed by hand --
# every id is prefixed with this machine's full home-directory path), so its output is
# inherently machine-specific, not portable, and not something that belongs in a public
# commit. Local build artifact, like target/ above. See
# tools/graphify.sh.
graphify-out/

# Per-machine harness settings, for the same reason graphify-out/ above is ignored:
# they name absolute tool paths on one workstation. The graphify hook-guard that was
# tracked here until 2026-08-02 pointed at a global `graphify` install that
# upstreams.toml's [graphify] entry deliberately excludes from Axon, so shipping it
# would have bound a public clone to exactly the uncontrolled version that entry
# argues against. The graphify *instruction* is project doctrine and stays in
# CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md; the binary path enforcing it is machine state.
# Only these two files: a project skill or agent under .claude/ is worth tracking and
# should still surface in `git status` rather than vanishing into an ignored directory.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
# Same class, written project-local by the graphify installer and regenerated by
# `tools/agent-integrations.sh install opencode`.
.opencode/

# PLAN.md is deliberately NOT ignored here any more (README.md#the-backlog-is-issues).
# Ignoring it is what let capabilities/PLAN.md grow into documentation ten tracked files
# cited while staying invisible to every gate. A stray plan file should show up as
# untracked in `git status` and get dealt with, not disappear.
to-integrate/
# Next.js build output
**/.next/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Static application output
**/dist/

# Vendored, committed build output — the one exception to the rule above. This is the
# SvelteKit browser client behind Accordion's Map, and it cannot be rebuilt from this
# tree (the build needs app/, which is not vendored). Upstream ships it in its npm
# package while never committing it to git; see Packs/harness/README.md.
!Packs/harness/pi-packages/accordion/extension/dist/
# SvelteKit generated output
**/.svelte-kit/

# Generated landing page (tools/generate-site) — built in CI and published, never committed.
site/

# The demo's recorded fixtures and the fictional vault tools/demo-seed writes (#168). Both are
# build products of the seeder plus the capability servers, regenerated by tools/demo-up. A
# tracked copy is the failure mode this whole design avoids: a stale recording published
# behind an API that had already moved, with nothing to notice it.
demo/fixtures/
demo/vault/
demo/state/

# Scouting's demo source declaration, generated by tools/demo-up from demo.toml's [demo] origin.
# Tracked, it would be the second place that port is written down — and the one that goes stale
# without anything failing. The overlay's machine.toml stays tracked and reviewable; this one
# file is a build product like the three above.
demo/overlay/config/scouting.json
# Comms' demo config, generated with a fresh throwaway API token on every run.
demo/overlay/config/comms.json
# Finance's demo instruments and target allocations, generated by tools/demo-up. Tracked,
# a hand-editable file at an overlay config path is the one shape in this tree where a real
# ISIN or a real allocation reaches the public repo with no gitignore to catch it, and
# tools/check-site-payload.sh matches neither pattern.
demo/overlay/config/finance.json
# Everything tools/demo-up and tools/demo-seed generate UNDER the demo overlay's data root,
# which since the decision ledger includes demo/overlay/data/finance/decisions/YYYY-MM.md:
# `tools/demo-seed.ts` posts to the api/decisions/run route and the export lands wherever
# SJEL_PERSONAL_ROOT points, which during a demo run is this directory. `git ls-files demo/overlay` returns one
# file and this is what keeps it that way.
demo/overlay/data/

# Agent worktrees created by Claude Code isolation (not repository content)
.claude/worktrees/

# The local-inference advisory gate writes one lock file beside the database.
# `local_gate::lock_path` falls back to the working directory when a config
# carries no database path, which is how one of these reached a commit once.
axon-local-*.lock

# Skill eval workspaces. tools/skill-eval writes one next to the skill it evaluates
# (<skill>-workspace/iteration-N/), which is where skill-creator's method says results live —
# next to the thing they are about. The outputs, timings and gradings are run artifacts, not
# source, so only the suite that produced them is committed.
*-workspace/

# Tauri plugin build output. `tauri-plugin` regenerates `.tauri/tauri-api` in every plugin, but
# only plugins/roomplan/.tauri is referenced: device-identity and foundation-models point their
# Package.swift at it so one Tauri runtime is linked. SwiftPM's own `.build`/`.swiftpm` are caches.
/plugins/device-identity/.tauri/
/plugins/foundation-models/.tauri/
/plugins/*/ios/.build/
/plugins/*/ios/.swiftpm/
/plugins/local-network/.tauri/
